WEBVTT

00:30.160 --> 00:33.880
Hey! You gave that to me, right?

00:38.350 --> 00:39.740
What're you doing?

00:39.740 --> 00:40.760
Give it back!

00:44.110 --> 00:46.310
It's better like this, isn't it?

01:01.400 --> 01:02.750
It's so nice!

01:03.240 --> 01:04.820
Not bad, I guess.

01:05.960 --> 01:07.420
Thanks, Kanon-chan!

01:08.290 --> 01:09.840
D-Don't mention it.

01:09.840 --> 01:12.090
It sure is nice, right, Urin?

01:12.940 --> 01:13.660
Does it look good?

01:13.660 --> 01:15.970
Little sisters, huh?

01:29.230 --> 01:31.770
kimi to ireba

01:29.230 --> 01:31.770
If I’m with you -

01:31.770 --> 01:34.610
kimi to itara

01:31.770 --> 01:34.610
because I’m with you -

01:34.610 --> 01:39.240
kokoro ga yasuraku

01:34.610 --> 01:39.240
my heart is at ease.

01:40.200 --> 01:42.790
kimi mo soude

01:40.200 --> 01:42.790
Surely, you’re the same.

01:42.790 --> 01:48.330
kimi mo ima yasurakerute

01:42.790 --> 01:48.330
You’re at ease now, too.

01:49.380 --> 01:55.970
itekuretara ii noni

01:49.380 --> 01:55.970
If you can just admit it,

01:57.720 --> 02:01.300
sono mama

01:57.720 --> 02:01.300
for even time to forget us,

02:02.220 --> 02:15.440
jikan saemo wasuresouna kurai shizen dakara

02:02.220 --> 02:15.440
it’s only natural, at this rate.

02:16.190 --> 02:26.910
yubisaki kara koboreochiru violet wo yo

02:16.190 --> 02:26.910
Violet drops, falling slowly from our fingertips…

02:26.910 --> 02:33.790
chiisana yume egaite yukou

02:26.910 --> 02:33.790
“Let us follow that small dream with a smile!”

02:33.790 --> 02:39.720
futaride sasayaka na

02:33.790 --> 02:39.720
And just like that, we are happy

02:41.140 --> 02:45.350
kotoba ga ureshii

02:41.140 --> 02:45.350
over such trifling words

02:45.850 --> 02:50.060
somatteku sora

02:45.850 --> 02:50.060
that paint the sky.

03:07.910 --> 03:12.880
The Heart that Covers the Light

03:40.030 --> 03:43.950
Big Solar Eclipse

03:42.950 --> 03:43.940
Solar eclipse?

03:44.420 --> 03:48.270
Yeah. Apparently, it's only seen once every several centuries.

03:48.270 --> 03:52.300
That's why so many people are coming here to Amamiko Island.

03:52.710 --> 03:54.380
Time to reel in some real money!

03:54.910 --> 03:56.540
Okay... What are these for?

03:56.790 --> 03:58.550
Stones that help you find love

03:57.000 --> 04:00.510
Stones that help you find love. Seashells that grant wishes.

03:59.050 --> 04:00.510
Seashells that grant wishes

04:00.940 --> 04:02.870
That's stupid.

04:02.870 --> 04:04.680
There's no way these things would-

04:06.310 --> 04:07.600
Welcome!

04:07.600 --> 04:08.540
Gimme!

04:08.540 --> 04:10.330
I want the stone that helps you find love!

04:10.330 --> 04:12.050
I want the seashell that grants wishes!

04:12.050 --> 04:13.020
Me too!

04:15.780 --> 04:18.220
What if I'm able to get a wonderful boyfriend with this?

04:20.660 --> 04:22.150
Perfect sales!

04:22.510 --> 04:25.620
Unbelievable! Why would they buy these kinds of things?

04:25.620 --> 04:29.330
Aren't the girl's hearts way too relaxed this summer?

04:29.330 --> 04:31.580
This required no capital since we just picked them up.

04:31.580 --> 04:33.550
That means free money!

04:33.550 --> 04:36.390
What an evil mother-daughter pair...

04:36.390 --> 04:39.320
All I did was help others find their happiness.

04:39.320 --> 04:40.710
Isn't that very pure?

04:40.710 --> 04:44.550
Evil is evil, but this kind of evil is so insignificant, anyway.

04:44.550 --> 04:46.230
Now's the perfect time to make money!

04:46.230 --> 04:48.370
I'll go and collect more stuff!

04:51.170 --> 04:52.640
Good grief.

04:54.390 --> 04:56.600
Solar eclipse, huh?

05:02.540 --> 05:06.830
I guess I really can't recall anything about eclipses at all.

05:06.830 --> 05:08.000
And, this is...

05:08.000 --> 05:12.200
This is an ancient writing about Sedona, written in the turtle language.

05:12.780 --> 05:16.050
This eclipse is not a mere coincidence.

05:16.050 --> 05:19.640
Sedona will not overlook this chance.

05:19.640 --> 05:23.850
She'll use the eclipse as a chance to gather large amounts of evil power.

05:23.850 --> 05:27.550
Sky Priestess, you especially must strengthen your heart.

05:27.850 --> 05:28.720
Me?

05:28.720 --> 05:32.520
If you're careless, I'm afraid that you might not be able to become a priestess again.

05:32.520 --> 05:33.650
Why is that?

05:33.650 --> 05:36.710
As long as you still have a sliver of evil in your heart,

05:36.710 --> 05:40.550
there is a possibility that you will be pulled into the darkness during the eclipse.

05:40.550 --> 05:41.400
What's with that?

05:41.870 --> 05:44.440
The light of your heart would cease to exist.

05:44.440 --> 05:47.860
What remained then would be a dark heart, filled with rage and hatred.

05:47.860 --> 05:51.160
You would not be able to feel love and happiness.

05:54.590 --> 05:56.810
What about the love we have toward someone?

05:58.200 --> 06:00.680
Of course, it would disappear as well.

06:07.170 --> 06:08.920
This is such nice weather,

06:10.320 --> 06:11.730
and there's the festival too.

06:13.820 --> 06:16.430
But somehow, I just don't feel like doing anything.

06:17.040 --> 06:20.400
Of course, since my rankings went down...

06:21.950 --> 06:23.810
Miyamori, you sure have it good, huh?

06:23.810 --> 06:25.330
You went up again, right?

06:27.960 --> 06:29.390
Well...

06:29.390 --> 06:30.490
You don't...

06:31.890 --> 06:34.870
You don't have to push yourself, you know?

06:35.570 --> 06:38.570
You want to say that it's my fault your rank dropped, right?

06:38.570 --> 06:40.920
Wait, I didn't mean it like that.

06:40.920 --> 06:43.350
That has to be it! Why don't you just be straight?

06:43.350 --> 06:46.090
I'm used to being told that anyway.

06:49.390 --> 06:50.670
Why...

06:51.820 --> 06:54.140
I don't mind even if you leave me.

07:00.820 --> 07:05.190
Even though he's the one who approached me...

07:11.100 --> 07:14.570
I think I'm better off without feelings of love someone.

07:14.570 --> 07:16.280
It's more convenient.

07:16.280 --> 07:18.440
Sounds normal, coming from the evil Sky Priestess.

07:18.440 --> 07:19.450
Is it really okay?

07:19.450 --> 07:23.130
The love you have toward your ex will disappear, you know.

07:23.130 --> 07:26.420
I told you that I couldn't care less about Kojima anymore, didn't I?

07:26.710 --> 07:30.220
Kojima? So he's called Kojima?

07:30.220 --> 07:32.440
Kojima, written as "small island."

07:32.440 --> 07:35.150
It's not like it matters anyway!

07:36.970 --> 07:38.100
It's okay!

07:38.510 --> 07:40.290
It's okay, Kanon-chan!

07:40.290 --> 07:40.650
What is?

07:40.650 --> 07:43.770
I'll be sure to protect the love inside Kanon-chan!

07:48.220 --> 07:49.740
No worries!

07:51.090 --> 07:53.660
You think I get what you're saying?

07:53.660 --> 08:00.790
Sea Priestess, during the eclipse, you have to make sure the Sky Priestess does not fall into the darkness.

08:00.790 --> 08:01.620
Got it?

08:01.620 --> 08:02.830
Yes!

08:03.840 --> 08:05.290
Let go! It's embarrassing!

08:05.290 --> 08:09.510
I'll take good care of this ring so Kanon-chan won't become evil.

08:09.870 --> 08:14.800
I am totally sure that the Sea Priestess has nothing to worry about, but...

08:14.800 --> 08:17.740
The Sky Priestess sure is worrying me.

08:17.740 --> 08:19.930
So much that I feel like I'll die soon.

08:21.440 --> 08:25.430
Elder of the Turtles, you shouldn't sigh. Your happiness will go away.

08:41.470 --> 08:44.310
We've heard this song before, I think.

08:44.310 --> 08:48.010
The people of the past went through many hardships.

08:48.010 --> 08:51.380
Although it was painful, they managed to overcome them

08:51.380 --> 08:53.140
by listening and dancing to this song.

08:53.140 --> 08:57.430
In the past, solar eclipses were seen as a sign of calamity, and thus were feared by the people.

08:57.430 --> 08:59.910
That's why this song is sung today.

08:59.910 --> 09:01.990
Of course, eclipses can be very surprising.

09:01.990 --> 09:04.600
The sun suddenly disappears and it becomes pitch black.

09:04.600 --> 09:05.900
Pitch black?

09:05.900 --> 09:09.230
Although it's still daytime, it's no brighter than the night.

09:10.610 --> 09:13.150
The light becomes darkness.

09:14.520 --> 09:17.070
Onee-chan, I'll always be with you!

09:15.730 --> 09:17.070
It ends very quickly though,

09:17.070 --> 09:18.730
so I don't think it's too significant.

09:18.730 --> 09:20.620
So, that's how it is!

09:20.620 --> 09:22.420
Kanon-chan, I love you!

09:22.420 --> 09:24.000
Okay, whatever.

09:24.410 --> 09:26.540
It sure is assuring to have Kanon-chan around, huh?

09:40.430 --> 09:43.720
In the past, Sedona rose from the sea to the sky.

09:43.720 --> 09:45.860
She brought the hearts of the Sky People into the darkness

09:45.860 --> 09:47.850
and covered the world with darkness.

09:49.340 --> 09:51.990
The last Sea and Sky Priestesses split Sedona into two halves

09:51.990 --> 09:55.940
and sealed them away in the sea and the sky.

09:56.580 --> 10:06.120
However, Urin accidentally released the sky-half of Sedona, and now it seeks to release the sea-half.

10:06.120 --> 10:07.750
Are you listening, Sam?!

10:07.750 --> 10:09.640
Of course I am.

10:09.640 --> 10:12.000
Anyway, Warin, you sure do know a lot about this, don't you?

10:12.000 --> 10:15.720
Didn't that Elder Turtle tell us about it when we went to the sky back then?

10:15.720 --> 10:17.410
Yeah. He did.

10:17.410 --> 10:19.520
You didn't listen to him, did you?

10:19.520 --> 10:22.430
Well... Anyway, what is Sedona?

10:22.430 --> 10:24.590
I don't think I can answer that,

10:24.590 --> 10:28.940
but if she completely revives herself, the world will be engulfed by darkness.

10:29.270 --> 10:31.170
Look, over there.

10:32.090 --> 10:35.750
Whoa, I can sense the evil feeling, even from here.

10:35.750 --> 10:40.070
Sedona's collecting the evil auras so she can use them to release her other half.

10:41.040 --> 10:44.850
If she manages to do so, the Sea won't be at peace anymore.

10:54.360 --> 10:57.070
Wow. So, it's finally begun.

10:57.070 --> 11:00.640
Amazing. The sun is really being blocked out.

11:03.300 --> 11:04.930
What now? Suzuki?

11:05.730 --> 11:06.960
It's Kojima.

11:06.960 --> 11:09.750
Why? What is it now? What does he want with me?

11:09.750 --> 11:10.770
You're not answering it?

11:10.770 --> 11:12.150
Well, it's Kojima!

11:16.630 --> 11:18.760
Why don't you call him back?

11:18.760 --> 11:21.140
There's no reason for me to do so, is there?

11:21.140 --> 11:23.370
What would I ask about anyway?

11:24.490 --> 11:27.100
Somehow, your words are no longer coherent.

11:27.100 --> 11:29.380
Not good! We can't let her become evil!

11:29.380 --> 11:31.310
Darkness is taking over her heart!

11:31.310 --> 11:32.070
But...

11:32.070 --> 11:34.230
You just have to say "I love you" to him.

11:34.230 --> 11:35.460
How could I say such a thing?

11:35.930 --> 11:36.960
You don't love him?

11:41.370 --> 11:42.650
I-I got it!

11:42.650 --> 11:46.490
It's not like I wanted that ring from Kojima anyway!

11:46.490 --> 11:48.370
Hey, Sky Priestess.

11:48.370 --> 11:49.580
You don't have to worry.

11:49.580 --> 11:51.840
It's not as if something like this can turn me evil.

11:51.840 --> 11:52.850
Really?

11:52.850 --> 11:56.390
If I hadn't kept this ring, you would've returned to being evil, right?

11:57.080 --> 11:58.190
I can't deny that.

11:58.190 --> 12:00.610
Wouldn't that be troubling?

12:00.610 --> 12:03.860
Jeez, Kanon-chan is too easily swayed by evil.

12:03.860 --> 12:05.570
Okay, I got it already!

12:05.570 --> 12:06.670
I'll be careful.

12:06.670 --> 12:08.440
You really are a dangerous one.

12:08.440 --> 12:09.450
Yeah, yeah.

12:09.450 --> 12:12.540
If you stay like this, Onee-chan will be troubled, okay?

12:12.540 --> 12:13.620
You're right.

12:13.620 --> 12:15.750
You have to pull yourself together, okay?

12:15.750 --> 12:16.290
Urin.

12:18.290 --> 12:19.250
Urin!

12:19.660 --> 12:21.670
Watch how you talk to the Sky Priestess!

12:23.130 --> 12:24.090
But I...

12:27.320 --> 12:28.510
What is this feeling?

12:28.510 --> 12:32.060
We're unable to give it our all
because you're pulling us down!

12:32.060 --> 12:32.870
That's not it!

12:32.870 --> 12:34.480
If you keep using such arrogant words,

12:34.480 --> 12:36.230
it'd be better to return to the Sea by yourself!

12:40.040 --> 12:41.390
S-Sorry...

12:42.150 --> 12:44.390
That's wrong... That's not it!

12:44.390 --> 12:46.870
You can't even protect yourself.

12:50.380 --> 12:52.000
Marin, what's with you?

12:52.850 --> 12:53.860
Urin?

12:58.120 --> 13:00.140
Urin, wait!

13:03.820 --> 13:05.250
Urin!

13:18.790 --> 13:22.320
She usually goes somewhere where there are no people in situations like this.

13:22.320 --> 13:25.920
Seeing happy people will only bother her more.

13:31.020 --> 13:36.370
That was the first time I've felt such an emotion.

13:36.370 --> 13:37.500
Such an emotion?

13:37.980 --> 13:41.670
A very weird emotion. One that I've never known before.

13:41.670 --> 13:44.120
I said some very mean things to Urin.

13:44.120 --> 13:47.090
Why did I say them?

13:47.090 --> 13:48.340
What should I do?

13:49.680 --> 13:52.760
Aren't siblings like that?

13:53.250 --> 13:56.100
Don't fights between siblings happen all the time?

13:56.570 --> 13:59.770
We've never done that before.

13:59.770 --> 14:01.540
You're kidding me. Not even once?

14:01.540 --> 14:03.140
No. Never.

14:06.050 --> 14:08.570
Now that's rare.

14:08.570 --> 14:09.450
You think so?

14:10.390 --> 14:12.100
Don't ask me.

14:12.100 --> 14:16.060
I'm an only child, so I'm not sure of it.

14:16.060 --> 14:18.360
I have to apologize to Urin.

14:21.410 --> 14:22.540
Let's search for her then.

14:27.260 --> 14:29.000
Well, Marin, you search that side.

14:29.000 --> 14:29.760
Okay.

14:31.920 --> 14:34.180
I wonder where she went.

14:34.550 --> 14:36.140
Who're you searching for?

14:36.850 --> 14:40.020
Ooshima... Just kill me.

14:40.330 --> 14:42.450
What do you want? I'm in a hurry.

14:42.450 --> 14:44.410
Looking for Kojima-kun?

14:44.410 --> 14:48.160
Yeah, right. Why would I do that?

14:48.160 --> 14:51.530
Well, Kojima-kun is my boyfriend now.

14:51.960 --> 14:54.370
Ooshima, written as "large island"

14:54.370 --> 14:56.250
and Kojima, written as "small island."

14:56.250 --> 15:00.330
The big island holds the small island with her monstrous love!

15:00.680 --> 15:02.620
What are you trying to say?

15:02.620 --> 15:06.430
I'm way better than you in looks, style, and personality.

15:06.430 --> 15:08.790
That "personality" part is false.

15:08.790 --> 15:10.760
She's way more evil than me.

15:09.840 --> 15:11.390
Kanon-chan!

15:12.430 --> 15:15.470
Seems like she's not on this side!

15:31.790 --> 15:33.100
I was defeated.

15:33.100 --> 15:34.760
It's my first defeat.

15:34.760 --> 15:38.610
I've been the best woman on this island ever since I was born.

15:38.940 --> 15:39.920
Who the hell is that?!

15:39.920 --> 15:41.040
I'm Marin.

15:40.180 --> 15:41.040
My friend!

15:41.040 --> 15:43.130
Miyamori's friend?

15:43.130 --> 15:44.700
No way!

15:44.700 --> 15:47.050
So that's why the solar eclipse happened.

15:47.050 --> 15:49.750
You're the reason the sun was blocked!

15:49.750 --> 15:50.870
Enough.

15:50.870 --> 15:52.020
We're in a hurry.

15:52.020 --> 15:55.900
Whatever. You'd better not start reminiscing and call Kojima-kun, okay?

15:55.900 --> 15:57.810
Eh? So Kojima-san is calling you again?

15:58.500 --> 15:59.140
What's that?

15:59.770 --> 16:02.000
No, it's nothing. He called the wrong number.

16:02.000 --> 16:03.480
And I didn't answer.

16:03.480 --> 16:04.820
We didn't talk or anything.

16:04.820 --> 16:05.560
Let's go.

16:15.280 --> 16:17.830
You don't wear the ring anymore, huh?

16:18.830 --> 16:20.820
How did you know about that?

16:21.310 --> 16:23.790
Of course I know. I chose it, after all.

16:24.240 --> 16:25.950
What? What do you mean?

16:25.950 --> 16:27.900
It doesn't really matter anymore, right?

16:27.900 --> 16:29.900
You two are already finished.

16:40.050 --> 16:42.580
No worries. They still can get bigger.

16:42.580 --> 16:44.900
I'm not fully grown yet!

16:53.650 --> 16:55.110
Onee-chan!

16:55.110 --> 16:57.640
Urin! I'm so glad!

16:57.640 --> 16:58.660
Urin!

16:58.980 --> 17:00.630
If you keep using such arrogant words,

17:00.630 --> 17:02.200
it'd be better to return to the Sea by yourself!

17:05.600 --> 17:07.320
Onee-chan...

17:08.080 --> 17:09.670
Oh, no. I'm sorry.

17:09.670 --> 17:11.000
You okay?

17:16.370 --> 17:17.720
I hate the sky.

17:17.720 --> 17:19.350
And the Sky People too!

17:19.350 --> 17:20.260
I hate everything about them!

17:20.970 --> 17:23.030
I want to go back to the Sea!

17:32.940 --> 17:34.500
It's about time!

17:52.290 --> 17:54.130
She's not here.

17:54.660 --> 17:56.630
We looked everywhere where there were no people.

17:56.630 --> 17:59.030
So she went into the crowd?

18:00.890 --> 18:03.140
It's kind of cold now, isn't it?

18:04.370 --> 18:05.770
Are you all right?

18:07.560 --> 18:09.980
Maybe it's because the sun is being blocked...

18:13.750 --> 18:16.860
The sun... It's amazing, isn't it?

18:17.460 --> 18:18.950
Oh, my! What is it?

18:21.060 --> 18:23.650
Say, Mama.

18:23.650 --> 18:26.700
Mama, listen to me.

18:26.700 --> 18:28.330
It's okay, it's okay.

18:35.260 --> 18:39.640
Urin and I... We were always together.

18:39.640 --> 18:42.300
I don't remember being separated even once.

18:42.300 --> 18:47.290
We were always together and we never fought.

18:48.770 --> 18:52.190
I wonder what went wrong.

18:54.400 --> 18:56.190
Isn't she just lonely?

18:56.970 --> 18:59.460
I mean, Urin's not a priestess.

18:59.460 --> 19:02.460
That's why I think she feels like she's being singled out,

19:02.460 --> 19:06.080
or that Marin won't be her sister anymore.

19:08.680 --> 19:11.120
Well, that certainly makes one feel lonely.

19:12.040 --> 19:14.960
You've noticed it already?

19:14.960 --> 19:17.090
I'm the one who's supposed to be her sister.

19:17.470 --> 19:20.070
Urin loves Marin so much,

19:20.070 --> 19:21.920
so I think if you just pat her head and say "it's okay, it's okay" to her,

19:21.920 --> 19:23.510
everything will be fine.

19:25.360 --> 19:26.890
I think you're right.

19:26.890 --> 19:28.430
While tightly hugging her too!

19:50.500 --> 19:51.970
Onee-chan, don't fight.

19:51.970 --> 19:52.850
I'm begging you!

19:52.850 --> 19:54.130
It's all right.

19:54.130 --> 19:55.710
You mustn't go anywhere, okay?

19:55.960 --> 19:57.380
Onee-chan!

19:58.050 --> 19:59.920
I'll never leave you.

20:00.490 --> 20:03.640
I'll always be Kanon-chan's friend.

20:13.880 --> 20:15.900
It's better like this, isn't it?

20:18.780 --> 20:20.900
It sure is assuring to have Kanon-chan around, huh?

20:22.750 --> 20:26.030
You can't even protect yourself.

20:52.070 --> 20:54.050
Don't you think it'd be better if we went home?

20:54.050 --> 20:59.480
No. We have to find Urin first.

21:34.300 --> 21:35.700
What?

21:49.730 --> 21:52.150
What's this feeling?

21:52.150 --> 21:54.160
Something's approaching this place.

22:26.650 --> 22:31.570
hikari no yurikago

22:26.650 --> 22:31.570
Within a droplet of water,

22:31.990 --> 22:35.120
shizuku no naka ni

22:31.990 --> 22:35.120
a cradle of light

22:35.450 --> 22:38.370
tojikometara

22:35.450 --> 22:38.370
is trapped.

22:38.370 --> 22:43.550
mizu no iro ni naru

22:38.370 --> 22:43.550
And so, it colors the water.

22:43.960 --> 22:47.170
mimi wo sumashite

22:43.960 --> 22:47.170
Clear your ears

22:47.170 --> 22:49.840
eien e

22:47.170 --> 22:49.760
to eternity.

22:49.840 --> 22:55.140
hitori de yume no ato

22:49.930 --> 22:55.140
Beyond a lonely dream,

22:55.140 --> 23:00.480
tsunaide yukeba

22:55.140 --> 23:00.480
if one connects with another,

23:01.190 --> 23:07.070
sotto kurikaesu kagayaki

23:01.190 --> 23:07.070
the repeating, soft shine

23:07.490 --> 23:12.120
warattemo attete

23:07.490 --> 23:12.120
meets and smiles,

23:12.120 --> 23:19.290
mou sukoshide kokoro ga todoku kara

23:12.120 --> 23:19.290
and with just a little more, the hearts have been reached.

23:19.290 --> 23:24.000
toumeina inori de

23:19.290 --> 23:23.880
With a transparent prayer,

23:24.000 --> 23:33.340
yasashiikuchikamu wo tsutsumuyo

23:24.000 --> 23:33.340
concealed within a gentle mouth.

23:35.510 --> 23:36.320
Did you know?

23:36.320 --> 23:38.980
It seems soapfish can hoot.

23:38.980 --> 23:40.810
Hoot, hoot!

23:40.810 --> 23:41.570
That's kind of cute, isn't it?

23:41.570 --> 23:43.010
But it's also poisonous!

23:43.010 --> 23:44.030
Then, it kills!

23:44.030 --> 23:45.770
Next up, episode six:

23:45.020 --> 23:49.860
The Falling Hearts

23:45.770 --> 23:47.300
The Falling Hearts.

23:47.300 --> 23:49.860
Everyone, I love you very much!
